<title>UK: Severn Trent slips amid downgrade talk.</title>
<headline>Severn Trent slips amid downgrade talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK water utility Severn Trent eased on Monday amid talk that NatWest had downgraded the stock, traders said.</p>
<p>The shares slipped 8-1/2p to 600p by 1135 GMT, against a generally rising market.</p>
<p>Traders said NatWest had downgraded its stance on Severn to &quot;reduce&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;. The broker was also said to have upgraded Thames Water, up 1-1/2p at 553p.</p>
<p>NatWest declined to comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
